Written by Spark 3.5.3 with Paimon 1.3.2.

id:int not null v:string
primary key: id
bucket: -1 (dynamic bucket)
dynamic-bucket.target-row-num = 2
deletion-vectors.enabled = true
file.format = parquet

CREATE TABLE dv (id INT, v STRING)
TBLPROPERTIES ('primary-key' = 'id', 'bucket' = '-1', 'deletion-vectors.enabled' = 'true',
               'file.format' = 'parquet', 'dynamic-bucket.target-row-num' = '2');

INSERT INTO dv VALUES (1, 'a'), (2, 'b'), (3, 'x'), (4, 'y'), (5, 'z');
-- snapshot 2: (1, a) (2, b) (3, x) (4, y) (5, z)
INSERT INTO dv VALUES (1, 'c'), (4, 'w');
-- snapshot 4: (1, c) (2, b) (3, x) (4, w) (5, z)
DELETE FROM dv WHERE id IN (2, 5);
-- snapshot 6: (1, c) (3, x) (4, w)

Keys are spread over several buckets, and each bucket keeps its own deletion vector index.
